b/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396606 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)={2}^{ax},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396606 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17d56701-363e-5629-ba43-f0ff54124002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396606 #edb/ref 1074 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$I$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, $f(x)={2}^{ax}>0$ for all $x\\in R$ for any $a\\in R,$ hence the zero function $z(x)=0\\notin I.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in I.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396607 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c7ef701a-1be0-572c-baca-f76e42023271" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396608 #edb/ref 1080 "addition of functions is not commutative" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396608 #edb/ref 